---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Bonfire — Ghost integration
description: Your readers can already reach you. Now they can reach each other. Bonfire's Ghost integration turns a publication into a community, without changing how you publish.
---
{# ============================================================
   V3 · GHOST INTEGRATION
   Frame: partnership, not comparison. Ghost publishes; Bonfire is where
   the publication becomes a place. Nothing on this page contrasts the two
   or implies something is missing from Ghost — every claim is additive.

   Structure: transformation · publisher tension · living publication ·
   Jacobin proof · integrated experience · fit and technical depth · start.

   TODO before launch:
     - confirm the extension repo URL (assumed bonfire_ghost)
     - groups are local-only for now (see features.njk), so the copy places
       the group as the local heart and federation as the outer ring
   ============================================================ #}

{% set repo = "https://github.com/bonfire-networks/bonfire_ghost" %}

{# shared class strings #}
{% set eyebrow = "flex items-center gap-3 font-smono text-[.72rem] font-bold tracking-[.18em] uppercase text-[var(--acc)]" %}
{% set display = "mt-[22px] font-disp font-[560] text-[clamp(1.7rem,3.2vw,2.6rem)] leading-[1.08] text-balance [font-variation-settings:'opsz'_96]" %}
{% set subhead = "font-disp font-[620] text-[clamp(1.15rem,2vw,1.4rem)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-.01em]" %}
{% set bodyp = "mt-5 text-[1.02rem] text-ink-2 max-w-[46rem] [&_b]:text-ink [&_b]:font-semibold" %}
{% set cellp = "text-ink-2 text-[.94rem]" %}
{% set kicker = "font-smono text-[.64rem] font-bold tracking-[.12em] uppercase text-ink-3" %}
{% set jump = "font-smono text-[.72rem] tracking-[.06em] text-ink-2 border border-ink/15 rounded-full px-3.5 py-[7px] hover:text-spark hover:border-flame" %}
{% set more = "inline-flex items-center gap-[9px] mt-[30px] pb-[3px] font-smono text-[.8rem] tracking-[.05em] text-spark border-b border-spark/35 hover:border-spark" %}
{% set btnfire = "btn h-auto min-h-0 rounded-full border-0 px-6 py-[.9rem] font-smono text-[.82rem] font-bold tracking-[.05em] text-[#221302] bg-gradient-to-br from-spark via-flame to-ember hover:from-spark hover:via-flame hover:to-ember shadow-[0_6px_26px_-8px_rgba(232,145,43,.55)]" %}
{% set btnline = "btn btn-ghost h-auto min-h-0 rounded-full px-6 py-[.9rem] font-smono text-[.82rem] font-bold tracking-[.05em] text-ink border border-ink/15 bg-ink/[0.03] hover:border-flame hover:text-spark hover:bg-ink/[0.03]" %}

{# feature table: a responsive two-column row that stacks on small screens #}
{% set trow = "grid grid-cols-1 min-[721px]:grid-cols-[minmax(0,15rem)_1fr] gap-x-8 gap-y-1 px-1 py-3.5 border-b border-ink/[0.07] last:border-b-0" %}

<div class="relative overflow-x-clip bg-night text-ink font-body leading-[1.58] antialiased selection:bg-ember selection:text-[#160c02]">
  <div class="v2-ambient" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="relative z-[1]">

    {# ---------- hero: one direct proposition ---------- #}
    <header class="flex min-h-[clamp(560px,70dvh,680px)] items-center border-b border-ink/[0.09]" style="--acc:var(--color-leaf)">
      <div class="w-full max-w-[1140px] mx-auto px-7 py-[clamp(64px,9vw,104px)]">
        <h1 class="mt-[18px] max-w-[16ch] font-disp font-semibold text-[clamp(2.15rem,5.6vw,4.8rem)] leading-[1.02] tracking-[0] text-balance [font-variation-settings:'opsz'_96]">Ghost publishing, with a community around it.</h1>
        <p class="mt-8 max-w-[43ch] text-[1rem] min-[601px]:text-[1.08rem] leading-[1.62] text-ink-2">Keep publishing as usual. Bonfire gives your readers a lasting place to meet between articles.</p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-[26px]">
          <a class="{{ btnfire }}" href="#reader-journey">See how it works</a>
          <a class="{{ btnline }}" href="/case-studies/jacobin/">Jacobin case study</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main>

    {# ============================================================
       PUBLISHER TENSION — recognition before product mechanics
       ============================================================ #}
    <section id="publisher-tension" class="py-[clamp(60px,8vw,104px)] scroll-mt-[70px]" style="--acc:var(--color-corn)">
    <div class="max-w-[1140px] mx-auto px-7">
      <div>
        <p class="{{ eyebrow }}"><i class="w-[9px] h-[9px] flex-none bg-[var(--acc)] [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></i>From publishing to participation</p>
        <h2 class="{{ display }} max-w-[850px]">A publication can have thousands of members and still have <span class="corn-text">nowhere they meet.</span></h2>
      </div>

      {% set tensions = [
        {
          icon: "ph-arrows-clockwise",
          title: "Every conversation starts again",
          text: "Comments capture the moment, but each new story starts another isolated conversation.",
          tone: "var(--color-corn)"
        },
        {
          icon: "ph-ticket",
          title: "Membership mostly opens content",
          text: "A paid tier opens articles and newsletters, but offers members few ways to contribute or connect.",
          tone: "var(--color-leaf)"
        },
        {
          icon: "ph-arrow-square-out",
          title: "Community lives somewhere else",
          text: "A chat server or commercial platform adds another account, interface and organisation to the relationship.",
          tone: "var(--color-flame)"
        },
        {
          icon: "ph-books",
          title: "The archive is rich but solitary",
          text: "Years of reporting remain readable, but rarely become living places where old and new conversations meet.",
          tone: "var(--color-spark)"
        }
      ] %}
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 min-[801px]:grid-cols-2 mt-[clamp(34px,4vw,52px)] border-t border-ink/15">
        {%- for item in tensions %}
        <article class="grid grid-cols-[2.25rem_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-4 min-[601px]:gap-5 py-6 min-[601px]:py-7 border-b border-ink/15 {% if loop.index % 2 == 0 %}min-[801px]:border-l min-[801px]:pl-8{% else %}min-[801px]:pr-8{% endif %}" style="--tone:{{ item.tone }}">
          <span class="grid w-9 h-9 mt-0.5 flex-none place-items-center text-[22px] text-[var(--tone)]" aria-hidden="true"><i class="ph-duotone {{ item.icon }}"></i></span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-disp font-[620] text-[1.12rem] min-[601px]:text-[1.2rem] leading-[1.2] tracking-[0]">{{ item.title }}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-[.93rem] leading-[1.58] text-ink-2">{{ item.text }}</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </div></section>

    {# ============================================================
       LIVING ARTICLE — the publication remains active between stories
       ============================================================ #}
    <section id="reader-journey" class="py-[clamp(64px,8vw,104px)] border-t border-ink/[0.07] scroll-mt-[70px]" style="--acc:var(--color-leaf)">
    <div class="max-w-[1140px] mx-auto px-7">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 min-[901px]:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(16rem,.55fr)] gap-8 min-[901px]:gap-[clamp(44px,7vw,92px)] items-end">
        <div>
          <p class="{{ eyebrow }}"><i class="w-[9px] h-[9px] flex-none bg-[var(--acc)] [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></i>A living publication</p>
          <h2 class="{{ display }} max-w-[720px]">What if every article <span class="corn-text">opened a room?</span></h2>
        </div>
        <p class="max-w-[34ch] text-[1rem] leading-[1.55] text-ink-2">Ghost remains the publishing home. Bonfire gives the people around it somewhere to stay.</p>
      </div>

      <figure class="aspect-[4/3] min-[901px]:aspect-[16/8] mt-[clamp(40px,5vw,60px)] overflow-hidden rounded-[6px] border border-ink/15 bg-[#ef0000]">
        <img class="w-full h-full object-cover object-center" src="/img/jacobin/ghostbonfire.png" alt="Jacobin's Ghost publication connected to its Bonfire community" width="2906" height="1729" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      </figure>

      {% set livingOutcomes = [
        { number: "01", text: "The discussion remains attached to the story.", tone: "var(--color-spark)" },
        { number: "02", text: "The subject becomes a place readers can return to.", tone: "var(--color-leaf)" },
        { number: "03", text: "Membership grows into participation.", tone: "var(--color-flame)" },
        { number: "04", text: "The community remains under your identity.", tone: "var(--color-corn)" }
      ] %}
      <ol class="grid grid-cols-1 min-[701px]:grid-cols-2 min-[1051px]:grid-cols-4 border-b border-ink/15">
        {%- for outcome in livingOutcomes %}
        <li class="py-6 min-[601px]:py-7 border-t border-ink/15 min-[701px]:px-7 min-[1051px]:px-6 {% if loop.index % 2 == 0 %}min-[701px]:border-l{% endif %} {% if not loop.first %}min-[1051px]:border-l{% endif %} {% if loop.index == 1 or loop.index == 3 %}min-[701px]:pl-0 min-[1051px]:pl-6{% endif %} {% if loop.first %}min-[1051px]:pl-0{% endif %}" style="--tone:{{ outcome.tone }}">
          <span class="font-smono text-[.66rem] font-bold tracking-[.12em] text-[var(--tone)]">{{ outcome.number }}</span>
          <p class="mt-2 max-w-[22ch] font-disp font-[580] text-[1.12rem] min-[601px]:text-[1.25rem] leading-[1.2] text-ink">{{ outcome.text }}</p>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ol>
    </div></section>

    {# ============================================================
       4 · IN THE WILD — Jacobin. Facts sourced from case-studies/index.njk;
       keep them in step if that page changes.
       ============================================================ #}
    <section id="wild" class="py-[clamp(56px,7vw,90px)] border-t border-ink/[0.07] scroll-mt-[70px]" style="--acc:var(--color-corn)">
    <div class="max-w-[1140px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="{{ eyebrow }}"><i class="w-[9px] h-[9px] flex-none bg-[var(--acc)] [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></i>In the wild</p>
      <h2 class="{{ display }}">Jacobin wanted more than <span class="corn-text">a comment section.</span></h2>
      <p class="{{ bodyp }}">Readers of Jacobin's German edition backed a publication they could not only read, but use to debate, organise and build solidarity together. Jacobin kept its Ghost workflow; Bonfire gave the community a home under Jacobin's identity.</p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 min-[901px]:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,26rem)] gap-px mt-[34px] rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-ink/15 bg-ink/15">
        <div class="bg-night">
          <img class="w-full aspect-[16/9] object-cover object-center" src="/img/jacobin/jacobin-social.png" alt="Jacobin Social, a federated community space for the German edition of Jacobin magazine" loading="lazy">
          <div class="px-[26px] py-7 min-[601px]:px-8 min-[601px]:py-8">
            <h3 class="{{ subhead }} mb-3">From audience to community</h3>
            <blockquote class="m-0 text-[1rem] leading-[1.65] text-ink-2">“Choosing Bonfire wasn't just a technical decision, it was a fundamentally political one. We wanted a platform that couldn't be switched off by a foreign government or bought out by a billionaire.”</blockquote>
            <p class="mt-3 font-smono text-[.7rem] tracking-[.05em] text-ink-3">Magdalena Berger · Jacobin DE</p>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-6">
              <a class="{{ btnfire }}" href="/case-studies/jacobin/">Read the full story</a>
              <a class="{{ btnline }}" href="https://jacobin.social" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit jacobin.social ↗</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <aside class="bg-night-3 px-[26px] py-7">
          {% set jstats = [
            { k: "Publication", v: "Jacobin — German edition" },
            { k: "Live since", v: "July 2026" }
          ] %}
          {%- for s in jstats %}
          <div class="pb-3 mb-3 border-b border-ink/[0.07]">
            <div class="{{ kicker }}">{{ s.k }}</div>
            <div class="text-[.98rem] text-ink mt-1.5">{{ s.v }}</div>
          </div>
          {%- endfor %}
          <div class="{{ kicker }}">What they switched on</div>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5 mt-3">
            {%- for t in ["federated comments", "Ghost integration", "membership sync", "groups &amp; topics", "their own branding"] %}
            <span class="font-smono text-[.66rem] text-corn-2 border border-corn-2/40 rounded-[7px] px-2 py-[5px]">{{ t | safe }}</span>
            {%- endfor %}
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>

      <a class="{{ more }}" href="/case-studies">See how other communities set theirs up →</a>
    </div></section>

    {# ============================================================
       5 · ONE INTEGRATED EXPERIENCE
       ============================================================ #}
    <section id="how-it-works" class="py-[clamp(64px,8vw,104px)] border-t border-ink/[0.07] bg-night-2/35 scroll-mt-[70px]" style="--acc:var(--color-leaf)">
    <div class="max-w-[1140px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="{{ eyebrow }}"><i class="w-[9px] h-[9px] flex-none bg-[var(--acc)] [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></i>One integrated experience</p>
      <h2 class="{{ display }} max-w-[800px]">Ghost publishes. Bonfire gives the publication <span class="corn-text">a place to gather.</span></h2>
      <p class="{{ bodyp }}">Your editorial team keeps one publishing system and one member relationship. Ghost remains the source of truth; Bonfire turns that foundation into a persistent community.</p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 min-[901px]:grid-cols-[1fr_auto_1fr] mt-[clamp(34px,5vw,52px)] border-y border-ink/15">
        <div class="py-7 min-[901px]:pr-10">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <i class="ph-duotone ph-article text-[24px] text-leaf" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <h3 class="{{ subhead }}">Ghost continues to handle</h3>
          </div>
          <ul class="mt-5 grid gap-3 pl-5 list-disc marker:text-leaf text-[.95rem] text-ink-2">
            <li>Writing, editing, publishing and newsletters</li>
            <li>Members, payments and membership tiers</li>
            <li>Article visibility and the publication website</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="hidden min-[901px]:block w-px bg-ink/15" aria-hidden="true"></div>

        <div class="py-7 border-t border-ink/15 min-[901px]:border-t-0 min-[901px]:pl-10">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <i class="ph-duotone ph-users-three text-[24px] text-corn" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <h3 class="{{ subhead }}">Bonfire adds</h3>
          </div>
          <ul class="mt-5 grid gap-3 pl-5 list-disc marker:text-corn text-[.95rem] text-ink-2">
            <li>Persistent discussions connected to articles</li>
            <li>Groups, topics, profiles and community relationships</li>
            <li>Participation and private spaces opened by membership</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      {# <div class="mt-[clamp(36px,5vw,56px)] grid grid-cols-1 min-[901px]:grid-cols-[minmax(0,.7fr)_minmax(0,1.3fr)] gap-8 min-[901px]:gap-14 items-start">
        <div>
          <p class="{{ kicker }}">What a member experiences</p>
          <h3 class="{{ subhead }} mt-3">One path from reading to belonging</h3>
        </div>
        {% set memberSteps = [
          { n: "01", title: "Read", text: "They open an article on the publication." },
          { n: "02", title: "Enter", text: "They use the email Ghost already knows." },
          { n: "03", title: "Participate", text: "Their membership opens the relevant discussion or space." },
          { n: "04", title: "Return", text: "People and subjects remain available after the story leaves the homepage." }
        ] %}
        <ol class="border-t border-ink/15">
          {%- for step in memberSteps %}
          <li class="grid grid-cols-[2.2rem_minmax(0,1fr)] min-[601px]:grid-cols-[2.2rem_7rem_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-x-3 gap-y-1 py-4 border-b border-ink/15 items-baseline">
            <span class="font-smono text-[.65rem] font-bold text-[var(--acc)]">{{ step.n }}</span>
            <strong class="font-disp font-[620] text-[1rem]">{{ step.title }}</strong>
            <span class="col-start-2 min-[601px]:col-start-auto text-[.93rem] text-ink-2">{{ step.text }}</span>
          </li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ol>
      </div> #}
    </div></section>

    {# ============================================================
       6 · FIT & TECHNICAL DEPTH
       ============================================================ #}
    <section id="fit-and-details" class="py-[clamp(56px,7vw,90px)] border-t border-ink/[0.07] scroll-mt-[70px]" style="--acc:var(--color-corn)">
    <div class="max-w-[1140px] mx-auto px-7">
      {# data first: the intro counts these, and nunjucks renders top-down #}
      {% set groups = [
        {
          icon: "ph-archive", title: "Articles",
          rows: [
            { k: "Full archive backfill", v: "A background job pages through every published article in your Ghost site." },
            { k: "Continuous import", v: "New articles arrive automatically as they're published." },
            { k: "Live updates", v: "Edits, visibility changes, unpublishing, deletion and republishing all follow through." },
            { k: "Faithful rendering", v: "Title, excerpt, HTML body, feature image, image metadata, original date and canonical URL." },
            { k: "Native article objects", v: "Real Bonfire Articles when the Articles extension is on, not posts pretending to be articles." },
            { k: "Duplicate-safe re-runs", v: "Canonical URLs match existing articles, so repeat imports update rather than multiply." },
            { k: "Tag filtering", v: "Import everything, or only articles carrying chosen primary or secondary Ghost tags." },
            { k: "Article browser", v: "Recent Ghost articles at /ghost, with images, excerpts, tags, dates and reading times." }
          ]
        },
        {
          icon: "ph-chats-circle", title: "Where discussion happens",
          rows: [
            { k: "A chosen destination", v: "Pick one group or topic, and every imported article lands there." },
            { k: "Destination checks", v: "The importing identity is verified as able to contribute to the destination you chose." },
            { k: "On-site comments embed", v: "One script tag in your Ghost theme renders the discussion under the article." },
            { k: "Fediverse participation", v: "With remote interaction enabled, people take part from another compatible server." },
            { k: "Durable discussions", v: "Conversations survive the source article being unpublished or deleted." },
            { k: "Author profiles", v: "Bylines become real profiles, with attribution that stays attached to them." },
            { k: "Embed can't be forged", v: "Author, destination and audience come from trusted settings, never from the embedding page." }
          ]
        },
        {
          icon: "ph-lock-key", title: "Access &amp; tiers",
          rows: [
            { k: "Visibility translation", v: "Public, members, specific tiers and paid each map onto Bonfire boundaries." },
            { k: "Tier circles", v: "Every Ghost tier mirrored as an instance-level circle named ghost_tier:&lt;slug&gt;." },
            { k: "Automatic protection", v: "Imported paid articles are gated by the matching tier with no extra setup." },
            { k: "Stale-grant removal", v: "Changing visibility or allowed tiers replaces old grants and clears dead permissions." },
            { k: "Archive, don't delete", v: "Retired Ghost tiers keep their circle and its history, marked archived." },
            { k: "Reusable anywhere", v: "Tier circles work throughout Bonfire's boundaries system, like any circle you'd make by hand." }
          ]
        },
        {
          icon: "ph-user-circle", title: "Accounts &amp; identity",
          rows: [
            { k: "Email-only sign-in", v: "A one-time link replaces password and local signup forms." },
            { k: "Ghost-gated eligibility", v: "An unknown address is checked against Ghost before any link is sent." },
            { k: "Tier gating", v: "Allow every member, or restrict new accounts to selected tiers. Any one match is enough." },
            { k: "Staff admission", v: "Active owners, admins, editors, authors and contributors get in without a tier." },
            { k: "Enumeration-proof", v: "Valid, unknown and ineligible addresses all receive the same neutral response." },
            { k: "Identity linking", v: "Member and staff records converge on one account, matched by Ghost ID first, email second." },
            { k: "Email-change tracking", v: "Ghost email changes are followed, unless the address was deliberately changed here." },
            { k: "No silent merges", v: "Conflicting identity or email records stay an administrator's decision, never an automatic one." }
          ]
        },
        {
          icon: "ph-gear-six", title: "Operations &amp; security",
          rows: [
            { k: "Admin dashboard", v: "Connection status, article counts, import rules, tier, member and staff lists in one screen." },
            { k: "Live sync reporting", v: "Progress counters, current stage, recent per-item errors, timestamps and stalled-job detection." },
            { k: "Resumable backfills", v: "Completed pages are checkpointed, so a retry picks up from durable progress." },
            { k: "Gated content support", v: "The Admin API supplies complete HTML for paid articles; the Content API covers public ones." },
            { k: "Idempotent syncs", v: "Re-running article, tier or member synchronisation is safe by design." },
            { k: "Signed webhooks", v: "HMAC-SHA256 over the original body and timestamp, with a five-minute replay window." },
            { k: "Fail closed", v: "No shared secret configured means no webhook is accepted, and invalid ones die before queueing." },
            { k: "Permission-gated data", v: "Member information and sync actions require instance-administration permissions." }
          ]
        }
      ] %}

      <p class="{{ eyebrow }}"><i class="w-[9px] h-[9px] flex-none bg-[var(--acc)] [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></i>Is this the right fit?</p>
      <h2 class="{{ display }}">Do you need more than <span class="corn-text">Ghost comments?</span></h2>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 min-[861px]:grid-cols-2 mt-[clamp(34px,5vw,50px)] border-y border-ink/15">
        <div class="py-7 min-[861px]:pr-9">
          <h3 class="{{ subhead }}">Ghost comments may be enough when</h3>
          <ul class="mt-5 grid gap-3 pl-5 list-disc marker:text-ink-3 text-[.95rem] text-ink-2">
            <li>Conversation only needs to happen underneath individual articles.</li>
            <li>Membership is mainly about access to content and newsletters.</li>
            <li>Readers do not need persistent profiles, groups or topic spaces.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="py-7 border-t border-ink/15 min-[861px]:border-t-0 min-[861px]:border-l min-[861px]:pl-9">
          <h3 class="{{ subhead }}">Bonfire becomes useful when</h3>
          <ul class="mt-5 grid gap-3 pl-5 list-disc marker:text-corn text-[.95rem] text-ink-2">
            <li>Discussions should continue across articles and publishing cycles.</li>
            <li>Membership should open participation, groups or private spaces.</li>
            <li>Readers, writers and the publication need lasting relationships.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-[clamp(48px,7vw,76px)]">
        <p class="{{ kicker }} text-[var(--acc)]">For your technical team</p>
        <h3 class="{{ subhead }} mt-3 text-[clamp(1.35rem,2.3vw,1.75rem)]">A deep integration, available for scrutiny.</h3>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[.98rem] text-ink-2 max-w-[46rem]">Nothing depends on maintaining duplicate editorial or member data by hand. Open an area to inspect what ships today.</p>
      </div>

      {# each group collapses; all closed on load. Pure CSS, no JS. #}
      <div class="grid gap-3 mt-[34px]">
        {%- for g in groups %}
        <details class="group/d rounded-xl border border-ink/15 open:border-ink/25 open:bg-night-2/40 transition-colors duration-200">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden flex items-center gap-3.5 px-[22px] min-[601px]:px-[26px] py-[18px] rounded-xl hover:bg-ink/[0.025]">
            <i class="ph-duotone {{ g.icon }} text-[22px] text-[var(--acc)]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <h3 class="font-disp font-[620] text-[1.1rem] min-[601px]:text-[1.15rem]">{{ g.title | safe }}</h3>
            {# counted from the data, so it can't drift — the depth signal while collapsed #}
            <span class="ml-auto hidden min-[521px]:inline font-smono text-[.62rem] tracking-[.1em] uppercase text-ink-3 whitespace-nowrap">{{ g.rows | length }} capabilities</span>
            <span class="flex-none ml-auto min-[521px]:ml-0 w-6 h-6 rounded-full border border-ink/20 flex items-center justify-center text-[.9rem] leading-none text-ink-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open/d:rotate-45 group-hover/d:border-[color-mix(in_srgb,var(--acc)_45%,transparent)]" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="border-t border-ink/15 px-[22px] min-[601px]:px-[26px] pt-2 pb-5">
            {%- for r in g.rows %}
            <div class="{{ trow }}">
              <div class="font-disp font-[620] text-[.99rem] text-ink">{{ r.k | safe }}</div>
              <div class="text-ink-2 text-[.94rem]">{{ r.v | safe }}</div>
            </div>
            {%- endfor %}
          </div>
        </details>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-7">
        <a class="{{ btnline }}" href="{{ repo }}#readme">Read the extension documentation</a>
        <a class="{{ more }} mt-0 self-center" href="{{ repo }}">Browse the source code →</a>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    {# ============================================================
       7 · CHOOSE HOW TO START — two paths, one closing. The Mosaic column
       is the primary CTA; the self-hosted column must never read as the
       lesser option, since it's the same AGPL code either way.
       ============================================================ #}
    <section id="start" class="py-[clamp(56px,7vw,90px)] border-t border-ink/[0.07] scroll-mt-[70px]" style="--acc:var(--color-flame)">
    <div class="max-w-[1140px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="{{ eyebrow }}"><i class="w-[9px] h-[9px] flex-none bg-[var(--acc)] [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></i>Getting started</p>
      <h2 class="{{ display }}">Build it with us or <span class="fire-text">run it yourself.</span></h2>
      <p class="{{ bodyp }}">It is the <b>same AGPL-licensed software</b> in both cases. The difference is how much implementation, hosting and co-design support your publication wants.</p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 min-[941px]:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-[34px] items-start">

        {# --- with us: Mosaic --- #}
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-flame/30 bg-[linear-gradient(160deg,rgba(245,195,68,.08),rgba(255,223,130,.03))] px-[26px] py-7">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 flex-wrap">
            <span class="font-smono text-[.66rem] font-bold tracking-[.12em] uppercase text-flame">Bonfire Mosaic</span>
            <span class="font-smono text-[.6rem] tracking-[.1em] uppercase text-ink-3 border border-ink/15 rounded-full px-2.5 py-[3px]">Most publishers start here</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="{{ subhead }} mt-3.5 mb-2.5">Build it with us</h3>
          <p class="{{ cellp }}">We shape the community around your publication, readers and rules, then connect Ghost, import the archive and prepare it for launch.</p>

          {% set mos = [
            "Community research, structure and governance.",
            "Ghost connection, tier sync and archive import.",
            "Your branding, language, onboarding and training."
          ] %}
          <div class="grid gap-2.5 mt-5">
            {%- for m in mos %}
            <div class="grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-3 text-[.93rem] text-ink-2">
              <i class="ph-duotone ph-check-circle text-[17px] mt-[3px] text-flame" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>{{ m }}</span>
            </div>
            {%- endfor %}
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-6">
            <a class="{{ btnfire }}" href="https://cal.com/bonfire-networks/meet">Book a call</a>
            <a class="{{ btnline }}" href="/mosaic">How Mosaic works</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        {# --- on your own --- #}
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-ink/15 px-[26px] py-7">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 flex-wrap">
            <span class="font-smono text-[.66rem] font-bold tracking-[.12em] uppercase text-ink-2">Self-hosted</span>
            <span class="font-smono text-[.6rem] tracking-[.1em] uppercase text-leaf border border-leaf/40 rounded-full px-2.5 py-[3px]">AGPL · free forever</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="{{ subhead }} mt-3.5 mb-2.5">Or do it yourself</h3>
          <p class="{{ cellp }}">A technically comfortable team can install the same open-source integration directly or work with a managed host.</p>

          {% set own = [
            "No licence fee, seat pricing or gated features.",
            "Public source and documentation.",
            "Self-hosted, managed, forkable and portable."
          ] %}
          <div class="grid gap-2.5 mt-5">
            {%- for o in own %}
            <div class="grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-3 text-[.93rem] text-ink-2">
              <i class="ph-duotone ph-terminal-window text-[17px] mt-[3px] text-leaf" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>{{ o }}</span>
            </div>
            {%- endfor %}
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-6">
            <a class="{{ btnline }}" href="/start">Install Bonfire</a>
            <a class="{{ btnline }}" href="{{ repo }}">The extension on GitHub</a>
            {# <a class="{{ btnline }}" href="/hosting">Managed hosting</a> #}
          </div>

        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="mt-[clamp(56px,8vw,92px)] pt-[clamp(48px,7vw,76px)] pb-[clamp(20px,3vw,36px)] border-t border-ink/15 text-center">
        <h3 class="mx-auto max-w-[25ch] font-disp font-[560] text-[clamp(1.75rem,3.5vw,2.7rem)] leading-[1.08] text-balance [font-variation-settings:'opsz'_96]">Your readers are already here. <span class="fire-text">Give them a place to belong.</span></h3>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-5 max-w-[52ch] text-[1rem] text-ink-2">Tell us what you publish, how readers participate today and what you would want them to do together. We will tell you honestly whether Bonfire fits.</p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3.5 mt-7">
          <a class="{{ btnfire }}" href="https://cal.com/bonfire-networks/meet">Tell us about your publication</a>
          <a class="{{ btnline }}" href="https://jacobin.social" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit Jacobin Social ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    </main>

  </div>
</div>
